<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iee06e50b7f99fe53f60d158f0871b6afed6087fd" commit="556b33c7f0b663996c2c70ab7cee7594077f324d" commit_message="Reintroduce kernel-next  Reintroduce kernel-next and point it to a branch in the kernel-next repository which will not be rebased. This ensures that the git history will not be overwritten.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:*696828  Change-Id: Iee06e50b7f99fe53f60d158f0871b6afed6087fd Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1276905 Reviewed-by: Ross Zwisler &lt;zwisler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1276905" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/05/1276905/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia0ca2101761cdb96af85eb25a6ef323385cf93ca" commit="ce0eb1690e58372c3c7f750e0f3d2d962ff73d5e" commit_message="Deprecate --create_bios_rw_image option  The `--create_bios_rw_image` is only used by RO-Normal firmware. With CL:*684050 and CL:*684108, we have migrated all chromeos-firmware-* packages using CROS_FIRMWARE_BUILD_RW_IMAGE (which leads to --create_bios_rw_image) to using new updater5 quirks and no longer needs to have RW blob created in packer.  BUG=chromium:882445 TEST=./pack_firmware_unittest.py; ./pack_firmware_functest.py  Change-Id: Ia0ca2101761cdb96af85eb25a6ef323385cf93ca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1255088 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1255088" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/88/1255088/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2d4673b7f02a2b3f5002c1bc291c8c8a0dc28bb8" commit="75c6a631ac5c3b4f711c75047fec8eebe1f26604" commit_message="updater: Remove unused file  - src/*:   The src/ contains files created for native updater (and no one   has used it yet); but in the end we moved the implementation to   platform/vboot_reference, so the file here is no longer needed.  - utils/decode_int32.py:   The decode_int32 was used only when we still have the shell script   based packer, to decode arguments. This has been replaced by   Python packer so it's also no longer needed.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I2d4673b7f02a2b3f5002c1bc291c8c8a0dc28bb8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1234096 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="1234096" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/96/1234096/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3ada731a2f761c40140e85f689b314895d048e2f" commit="cc5ec7e4b350acc20ff4511b2b6109942791aed6" commit_message="[autotest][cfm] Migrates the CfM perf test to use bond  Changes include: - every perf run starts a new meeting instead of joining the same one - starting a meeting session now returns the meeting code - bot count has been reduced to 20   - after a f2f discussion with dancarregosa@ about the test case we concluded there was no difference between 20 and e.g. 50 for this use case - 1 bot now sends audio to cause more load - 1 bot now pins the CfM to enforce HD  BUG=b:116194847 TEST=local setup  Change-Id: I3ada731a2f761c40140e85f689b314895d048e2f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1276525 Commit-Ready: Denis Tosic &lt;dtosic@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Denis Tosic &lt;dtosic@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kristoffer Erlandsson &lt;kerl@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1276525" owner_email="dtosic@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/25/1276525/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2ae39e2db4b1a01ec5ec9855634357434f01020b" commit="a703173d397b3fbdff6737636639780137de39e2" commit_message="cr50: Only allow SN hash to be written if board ID is not set.  This should restrict SN hash such that is can only be written at factory (before board id), with the exception of some edge cases where devices that have left factory do not have a board id set.  BUG=b:111195266 TEST=tested locally on soraka BRANCH=none  Change-Id: I2ae39e2db4b1a01ec5ec9855634357434f01020b Signed-off-by: Louis Collard &lt;louiscollard@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1237696 Reviewed-by: Andrey Pronin &lt;apronin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1237696" owner_email="louiscollard@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/96/1237696/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="I2b295cb6b36bf2853240276b6e2e52d8e56466a3" commit="1c36961c7b63e16981470704e575ef8291693309" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: disable CONFIG_EFI for arm64  The config CONFIG_EFIVAR_FS=m cause bvt-inline test (kernel_ConfigVerify) to fail, and we're not going to use EFI. Disable the config.  The change is generated from the following commands:  cat &lt;&lt;EOF | tee -a \     chromeos/config/arm64/chromiumos-arm64.flavour.config \     chromeos/config/arm64/chromiumos-mediatek.flavour.config  CONFIG_EFI=n  EOF  ./chromeos/scripts/kernelconfig olddefconfig  BUG=b:117193994 TEST=test_that &lt;dut&gt; kernel_ConfigVerify TEST=manually on DUT.  Change-Id: I2b295cb6b36bf2853240276b6e2e52d8e56466a3 Signed-off-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1270503 Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1270503" owner_email="pihsun@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/03/1270503/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.14" change_id="Id54d37d18ac66c6c76631e122e7f3e4133719c40" commit="fdacb1cd5487b8d19cd7cb684ce5f277cef7ecea" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-cheza: Enable uart6  Enabling uart6 (used for Bluetooth) for cheza consists in multiple smaller changes:  - mark the UART as enabled - extend the sdm845 pinctrl config for uart6 to include the RTS/CTS lines - configure the drive strength for the default config - add 'hsuart' alias for uart6 to keep the GENI serial driver happy  BUG=b:79942381 TEST=the kernel can communicate with the Bluetooth chip  Change-Id: Id54d37d18ac66c6c76631e122e7f3e4133719c40 Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1274067 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1274067" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/67/1274067/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie718e7a7e14606f01f7fc934c8f8c7ece0e63be0" commit="abc76ced226aeb03932e5c089b73026921eaad72" commit_message="pack_firmware: Keep extra firmware images in top level folder.  The signer bot does not process bin/*.bin, but currently all files listed in EXTRA (which will be copied by CopyElfs) will live in bin/ sub folder.  &quot;Extra firmware images&quot; is eliminated in M71+, so we want some simple work around for M69 and M70, by copying files directly if the file name looks like *.bin.  BUG=chromium:894324 TEST=Revert CL:*684050, then run: emerge-daisy chromeos-firmware-daisy;      chromeos-firmwareupdate -V | grep '\.bin'      # 7f5b0669d9f43b0075cded5688a0a343 *./bios-snow-2695.132.ro.bin      # 673c3efd476ac9a803cfc2f724c24806 *./bios_rw.bin      # 0d2c9045017a843ad16d492897481d88 *./ec-2695.132.bin      # 3849d1915bc50fb1a9a168c648517d37 *./bios-snow-2695.132.rw.bin      # e9306cb76c8e636b4f5847cc7702abe7 *./bios.bin  Change-Id: Ie718e7a7e14606f01f7fc934c8f8c7ece0e63be0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1275766 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1275766" owner_email="hungte@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/66/1275766/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I94126fdc541f9456c8f48f42383bc6e2188257e2" commit="f38669124d393b16353f4afdc906bfe2a2c941c5" commit_message="max17055: Support alert function.  MAX17055 support 4 kinds of alert: voltage, current, state-of-charge, and temperatore. This CL enables this functionality.  datasheet: https://datasheets.maximintegrated.com/en/ds/MAX17055.pdf  TEST=manually test on Kukui. BUG=b:111378620 BRANCH=None  Change-Id: I94126fdc541f9456c8f48f42383bc6e2188257e2 Signed-off-by: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1276006 Commit-Ready: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yilun Lin &lt;yllin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1276006" owner_email="yllin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/06/1276006/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iee40b4bedb76f90179eb73694b5713ceceb4bc2d" commit="4507d7ebad3e45842821e7d209eb5855acaaa35d" commit_message="cros-disks: Tighten capabilities  It turns out that we are running quite a few subprocesses without restricting capabilities, so these inherit cros-disks' comparatively powerful capabilities. This change restricts capabilities as much as possible in the current status quo.  BUG=chromium:866377,chromium:867509 TEST=Passes platform_CrosDisks{Filesystem,Format,Rename,Archive}  Change-Id: Iee40b4bedb76f90179eb73694b5713ceceb4bc2d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1276166 Commit-Ready: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mattias Nissler &lt;mnissler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1276166" owner_email="mnissler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/66/1276166/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I437e086809db734a789fa4b5ee7ecba7ba3bc1b1" commit="eafc8aefd8c307699fcb238db4ae81ed941fc399" commit_message="video_PlaybackPerf: Fail if an error occurs in HW playback  Originally, video_PlaybackPerf doesn't check an error status of VDA when HW playback is used. There is case that playback is fallback to SW when VDA causes an eror. In the case, SW playback performance values are reported as HW playback ones. This fails video_PlaybackPerf if an error in VDA occurs.  BUG=None TEST=video_PlaybackPerf on nyan_big and veyron_minnie  Change-Id: I437e086809db734a789fa4b5ee7ecba7ba3bc1b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1278605 Commit-Ready: Hirokazu Honda &lt;hiroh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hirokazu Honda &lt;hiroh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuo-Peng Liao &lt;deanliao@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1278605" owner_email="hiroh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/05/1278605/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id531508d865bff26b0ac97c08685b171c2d14c1d" commit="228fda4d15e172eb4e9dd5e4e8c54493da64f85a" commit_message="camera3_test: add camera_ids, camera_facing option  Add &quot;--camera_ids&quot; option for filter specific test camera id and &quot;--camera_facing&quot; option for test specific camera facing.  BUG=b:79951967 TEST=Run 'cros_camera_test' with --test_camera_ids option or --camera_facing, see if total number of run testcases change.  Change-Id: Id531508d865bff26b0ac97c08685b171c2d14c1d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/1161849 Commit-Ready: Kuo Jen Wei &lt;inker@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kuo Jen Wei &lt;inker@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shik Chen &lt;shik@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="1161849" owner_email="inker@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/arc-camera" ref="refs/changes/49/1161849/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="11150.0.0-rc5"/></manifest>